From: "Jose M. Caballero Guerrero"
 <80172778+Caballero-git@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 21:43:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 26/30] arm64: dts: rockchip: P25T: RK817 LDO2 at 1.2 V for the
 rear camera

The stock DT keeps RK817 LDO_REG2 ("vdda_0v9") at 1.2 V, always-on.
Our boot left it at its reset value of 0.9 V. The GC5035 then answers
on I2C and works from its 24 MHz input clock, but its logic freezes as
soon as it switches to its PLL, so it never streams. At 1.2 V the
unchanged driver delivers clean frames. Values copied from the stock DT.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0156c5MfQpFxaYWNNLMrcym9
---
 .../boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-teclast-p25t.dts | 26 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-teclast-p25t.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-teclast-p25t.dts
index b8cd10374..99c987f29 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-teclast-p25t.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-teclast-p25t.dts
@@ -607,6 +607,28 @@ regulator-state-mem {
 				};
 			};
 
+			/*
+			 * Camera core supply (patch 0030, Jose's OK 2026-10-07).
+			 * Stock LDO_REG2: named "vdda_0v9" but set to 1.2 V,
+			 * always-on - values verbatim. Our boot left it at the
+			 * reset value 0.9 V: the GC5035 then answers on I2C and
+			 * runs from its 24 MHz input, but its logic freezes the
+			 * moment it switches to its PLL (0xfc = 0x8e), so it never
+			 * streams. At 1.2 V the unchanged driver delivers clean
+			 * frames (tests/test_22.sh .. test_45.sh, findings.org).
+			 */
+			vdda_0v9: LDO_REG2 {
+				regulator-name = "vdda_0v9";
+				regulator-min-microvolt = <1200000>;
+				regulator-max-microvolt = <1200000>;
+				regulator-always-on;
+				regulator-boot-on;
+
+				regulator-state-mem {
+					regulator-off-in-suspend;
+				};
+			};
+
 			/*
 			 * Audio codec IO/analog supply (patch 0015). Stock's own
 			 * LDO_REG4 is named "vccio_acodec" and is the vccio1-supply
@@ -910,7 +932,9 @@ spk_amp_enable_h: spk-amp-enable-h {
  * from CLK_CIF_OUT on GPIO4_C0 (pin group cif_clk, muxed in stock by
  * rkisp-vir0), pwdn GPIO4_B2 driven high to run, power domain PD_VI, no
  * supplies listed. Supplies here: avdd = LDO9 vcc2v8_dvp, dovdd = LDO8
- * vcc1v8_dvp, dvdd = vcc_camera (GPIO4_A7 switch). Stock routes the
+ * vcc1v8_dvp, dvdd = vcc_camera (GPIO4_A7 switch). The sensor core also
+ * needs RK817 LDO2 at 1.2 V as in stock (patch 0030; at 0.9 V its PLL
+ * clock domain freezes) - exact wiring unknown. Stock routes the
  * sensor through the D-PHY in split mode (csi2-dphy1 = lanes 0-1)
  * straight into the ISP; the CSI-2 host and VICAP are disabled there.
  * The front GC02M2 sits on lanes 2-3 (split mode, not in mainline) and
